# A bare pattern here only matches at the repo root — unlike
# .gitignore, .dockerignore does NOT recurse a plain "node_modules/"
# into subdirectories. Every entry that also needs to match nested
# copies (web/node_modules, apps/*/__pycache__, etc.) is written with
# a "**/" prefix so it actually does. Getting this wrong is why the
# backend image's build context was silently ~1GB (web/node_modules +
# web/.next) even though both looked "excluded" here.
.git
**/.gitignore
.env
.env.local
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
docs/
README.md
LICENSE
JUDGING.md
DATA-MODEL.md
